    "physical_description": "Hanging (suzani) of cotton embroidered with silks. Composed of five vertical strips embroidered in cerise, rust, beige, green, yellow, brown and blue. Bukhara couching, chain, broad chain, open chain and crested chain stitches. The border is divided into diamond and triangular-shaped compartments by elongated and serrated leaves. Within the diamonds are large lily flowers alternating with round eight-petalled flowers. Smaller round-head flowers fill the triangles.\r\n\r\nThe centre is decorated with four large floral sprays which form oval medallions extending inwards from the four corners. The four sprays are all different, with the curving and branching stems bearing two varieties of the lily, one with a carnation and one with a round-headed flower. Arranged over the remainder of the ground are 19 upright plants and leaf forms, all with slender curving stems and small leaves.\r\n\nLined with plain cotton and bordered, on the back, with strips of silk and cotton ikat.",
